  "problem": "If ${X}_{1}∼N(8,{40}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(30,{30}^{2})$ are independent and $Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2},$ calculate $P(-31\\le Y\\le 31).$ Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3557\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3520\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3483\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3936\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3897\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3859\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4325\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4286\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4247\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8289\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8315\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8340\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.0\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8531\\,$ </td><td align=